  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14267656/assets/5253ff44a3fb04cc09568e5289dd7e73d3e286651e257cf7efe20944ac57e439.png)\n\nThe function $f$ is part of the graph of the function $y=2\\sqrt{x}+1,$ as shown in the figure above. Find the number of months $x$ at which the inflation given by this function was $3\\,%.$\n\n*Hint: Remember that $f$ is measured in $%.$*\n\n$x\\,=\\,$\n{{field-1}}",
